/** @mainpage Qore XML Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section xmlintro XML Module Introduction

    The xml module provides <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/">XML</a>,
    <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-1/">XML Schema</a>, <a href="https://xmlrpc.com/spec.md">XML-RPC</a>,
    <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SOAP">SOAP</a> web service and
    <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4918">WebDAV</a> support for %Qore. Its XML processing is based on
    the <a href="https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2">libxml2</a> library, which the module can build as a
    private copy that includes the corrections it needs for standards conformance.

    Key capabilities:
    - conversion between %Qore data and XML documents without data loss: element order, mixed content, whitespace,
      comments, CDATA and embedded XML fragments can be retained (see @ref xmlserialization)
    - validation with <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-1/">XML Schema 1.0</a> (Parts
      <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-1/">1</a> and <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/">2</a>),
      <a href="https://relaxng.org/spec-20011203.html">RELAX NG</a> and XML 1.0 DTDs, for complete documents and
      while streaming (see @ref xmlschemavalidation)
    - streaming and SAX processing of large documents and input streams, one element at a time, with validation
      while reading (see @ref xmlstreaming)
    - DOM access and <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xpath-10/">XPath 1.0</a> queries, and
      <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xml-names/">XML namespaces</a>
    - secure parsing: external entities are never loaded, and entity expansion is bounded
    - <a href="https://xmlrpc.com/spec.md">XML-RPC</a> serialization, clients and a server handler (see
      @ref xmlrpcguide)
    - SOAP web services described by <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/2001/NOTE-wsdl-20010315">WSDL 1.1</a>, with
      <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/2000/NOTE-SOAP-20000508/">SOAP 1.1</a> and SOAP 1.2
      (<a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12-part1/">Part 1</a> and
      <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12-part2/">Part 2</a>) bindings: clients, a server handler and data
      providers, with SOAP encoding and faults, <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/SOAP-attachments">SOAP with
      Attachments</a>,
      <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/soap12-mtom/">MTOM</a>/<a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xop10/">XOP</a>
      and <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/ws-addr-core/">WS-Addressing 1.0</a> (see @ref xmlsoapguide)
    - a <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4918">WebDAV (RFC 4918)</a> server handler meeting compliance
      classes 1 and 2, and WebDAV clients (see @ref xmlwebdavguide)
    - data providers for SOAP services, WebDAV resources, SAX XML processing, cargo messages and HL7 CDA documents
      (see @ref xmlusermodules)

    @section xmlnavigation Documentation

    - @subpage xmlgettingstarted -- parsing, generating, validating and querying XML in a few lines
    - @subpage xmlserialization -- how %Qore data and XML are converted, and the generation options
